    {
      "access": "authenticated",
      "component": "host",
      "doc": "RAM is the scarce resource on these chips, so the host reports it to any module that asks. \"Largest block\" is the biggest\nsingle allocation that would succeed now; a heap can have plenty free and still refuse a request (fragmentation). Free\nmemory is tracked, not only reported: `lowest_free` shows the worst moment since boot, which is the number to size things by.",
      "index": 45,
      "method": "heap_info",
      "name": "host.heap_info",
      "request": {
        "fields": []
      },
      "response": {
        "fields": [
          {
            "description": "Free bytes.",
            "name": "free",
            "tag": 1,
            "type": "u32"
          },
          {
            "description": "The largest block an allocation can get now.",
            "name": "largest",
            "tag": 2,
            "type": "u32"
          },
          {
            "description": "The lowest free count since boot.",
            "name": "lowest_free",
            "tag": 3,
            "type": "u32"
          },
          {
            "description": "Total bytes of the heap.",
            "name": "total",
            "tag": 4,
            "type": "u32"
          },
          {
            "description": "Free internal RAM.",
            "name": "free_internal",
            "tag": 5,
            "type": "u32"
          },
          {
            "description": "The largest internal block.",
            "name": "largest_internal",
            "tag": 6,
            "type": "u32"
          }
        ]
      },
      "summary": "Free memory of the device",
      "visibility": "public"
    },
    {
      "access": "authenticated",
      "component": "host",
      "doc": "Built-in records are read during the call; contributed records (a component's `info_publish`) are cached and may be stale.\nThis call never invokes another module. No console module is needed. No partial record is returned on buffer overflow.",
